    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This CD-ROM contains descriptions and photos of mines, mine waste dumps, mills, and mill tailings and interim interpretations of their significance as sources of acid or metals in the upper Animas River watershed, San Juan County, Colorado.  Geochemical studies undertaken on these mining-related materials are part of broader integrated geologic, hydrologic, and biologic studies of the watershed that are underway to provide scientific rationale for effective reclamation of mine sites or restoration of aquatic habitat (Nimick and von Guerard, 1998). Information presented here should be used in conjunction with the reports by Nash (1999a, 1999b) that describe historic mine sites on U.S. Forest and U.S. BLM lands and an interim ranking of their priority for reclamation.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
